<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta http-equiv="X-UA-Compatible" content="IE=edge" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>What Is Far Reach Co? Virtual Tabletop, Campaign Hub, and Radio</title>
  <meta name="description" content="Far Reach Co. combines fast virtual tabletop sessions, persistent campaign management in Wyrlds, and Far Reach Radio for synced tabletop audio streaming." />

  <!-- Open Graph / Facebook -->
  <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
  <meta property="og:url" content="https://farreachco.com/what-is-frc" />
  <meta property="og:title" content="What Is Far Reach Co? Virtual Tabletop, Campaign Hub, and Radio" />
  <meta property="og:description" content="Fast virtual tabletop, persistent campaign tools in Wyrlds, and synced tabletop audio streaming with Far Reach Radio." />
  <meta property="og:site_name" content="Far Reach Co." />

  <!-- Twitter -->
  <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary" />
  <meta name="twitter:title" content="What Is Far Reach Co? Virtual Tabletop, Campaign Hub, and Radio" />
  <meta name="twitter:description" content="Fast virtual tabletop, persistent campaign tools in Wyrlds, and synced tabletop audio streaming with Far Reach Radio." />

  <!-- JSON-LD Structured Data - Multiple FAQs -->
  <script type="application/ld+json">
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [{
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is Far Reach Co?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Far Reach Co. is a virtual tabletop and campaign management platform built for Dungeon Masters who want fast, intuitive tools that stay out of the way. Start using the platform immediately with no upfront cost. Optional subscriptions unlock additional storage plus campaign presentation features such as Wyrld banners and public listing controls. It features a platform-agnostic VTT, D&D 5E character sheets, private campaign environments called Wyrlds, and a complete SRD reference."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Who is Far Reach Co for?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Far Reach Co. is designed for Dungeon Masters and Game Masters who value simplicity over feature bloat. It's for DMs who want to get a game running quickly, keep players immersed in the story rather than fighting the software, and prefer straightforward tools that just work. It's ideal for both new DMs learning the craft and experienced DMs tired of overcomplicated platforms."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do players need an account to join a Far Reach Co game?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No. For quick games and one-shots, players can join any table instantly with just a share link - no account, no signup, no friction. For ongoing campaigns using the Wyrld system, players create accounts to access persistent features like linked character sheets and campaign resources."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What problems does Far Reach Co solve?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Far Reach Co. solves common VTT frustrations: slow setup times, forced account creation for all players, restrictive asset upload policies, cluttered interfaces, and poor performance on slower connections. It offers zero-friction player joining, unrestricted image uploads, a clean focused interface, and fast load times even for players with limited bandwidth."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can I upload my own images to Far Reach Co?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Far Reach Co. allows you to upload any image you own for use as tokens, maps, or assets. There are no marketplace restrictions or format limitations. Use your own artwork, commissioned pieces, or any images you have the rights to use."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the difference between Dashboard tables and Wyrlds?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Dashboard tables are personal virtual tables ideal for quick games and one-shots. Anyone can join via share link without an account. Wyrlds are persistent campaign environments for ongoing games where players create accounts to link character sheets, access shared resources, and maintain campaign continuity across sessions. Wyrlds also support public discovery settings, featured onboarding records, and community discussion boards."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What are Public Wyrlds?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Public Wyrlds are campaign spaces that a Wyrld owner chooses to list in the directory. Guests and logged-in users can browse listings and read the selected featured record for onboarding context. Owners can keep joining invite-only or accept requests to join, and can set capacity limits."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Does Far Reach Co work on slow internet connections?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Far Reach Co. is built for fast load times and responsive performance, even on slower connections. The platform is kept lightweight so players aren't left waiting while the rest of the group moves on."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  </script>

  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css" />
